message: "If you use this research record, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LEBRE research record — v0.52-r1"
version: "v0.52-r1"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lima"
    given-names: "Silvano"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3868-6747"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Iquitim/lebre-research"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research record of LEBRE, an online one-step-ahead forecaster for time series
  with inputs, designed for a budget of a few hundred floating-point operations
  per step, in which each structural change is accepted by an anytime-valid
  sequential test (e-process) of predictive improvement. Contains the Python
  reference implementation, a C99 port with simulated Cortex-M4F measurements,
  experiment scripts, pre-registrations, results, frozen versions with SHA-256
  manifests and the v0.52 specification (revision 1).
keywords:
  - online forecasting
  - anytime-valid inference
  - e-process
  - online multiple testing
  - TinyML
  - reproducibility
